      <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">Loan EMI (Equated Monthly Installment) is computed using the annuity formula: <code>EMI = P × r × (1 + r)^n / ((1 + r)^n - 1)</code>, where <strong>P</strong> is the principal loan amount, <strong>r</strong> is the monthly interest rate (annual interest rate ÷ 1200), and <strong>n</strong> is the loan tenure in total months.</p>
