    <!-- Common Mistakes Section -->
    <section style="margin: 2.5rem 0;" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
      <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common Loan &amp; Mortgage Calculation Pitfalls</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li><strong>Focusing Only on Monthly Payment:</strong> Extending loan tenure lowers your monthly payment but drastically balloons total lifetime interest charges. Always evaluate total loan cost alongside monthly cash flow.</li>
        <li><strong>Confusing APR with Base Interest Rate:</strong> An annual percentage rate (APR) includes lender fees, points, and closing costs, whereas the nominal note rate dictates your exact monthly amortization calculation.</li>
        <li><strong>Assuming Equal Principal Reduction:</strong> During the early years of a loan, the vast majority of each payment goes toward interest. Principal reduction accelerates only in the latter half of the amortization schedule.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
